-- title:
--   Minimality of the Igusa branch at a crossing node
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5\le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q$ lying over $q$, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element whose image lies in $A$, and assume the contraction $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, is Henselian, has algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Give $\overline F:=\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the intermediate field $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M',\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series, the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\subseteq\overline F$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\overline F/k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ which contracts to $A$ on $k_0$ (for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff its image lies in $W_0$), is a discrete valuation ring, and has maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; for every subring $O\subseteq F_0$ which is local and noetherian, satisfies $O\subseteq W_0$, contracts to $A$ on $k_0$, has the property that each $f\in O$ differs from the image of some $x\in k_0\cap A$ by a nonunit of $O$, and has $F_0$ as its field of fractions (each $f\in F_0$ is $g/h$ with $g,h\in O$, $h\ne0$); for every $E_0\ge1$, with the image of $\pi_0$ in $O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ of the $\mathfrak m_{A_0}$-adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ at the parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$ (the quotient of $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]$ by `uvCrossingIdeal`), and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that quotient, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$, $\iota$ carries the image of each $x\in k_0\cap A$ to the corresponding constant `const`, $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$; and for every valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$ which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal — then every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ containing $O$ with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal satisfies $W_x\subseteq V$.
--
--   This is the canonicity, or minimality, of the Igusa branch at a node of the reduction: among all valuation subrings of the function field containing the local ring $O$ of a crossing-presented node and separating $\pi_0$ from $c_y$, the branch $W_x$ cut out by $c_x$ is the smallest. It is used in the construction of the node centres and layered node rings at a node of the Igusa curve.
